---
title: Primitive arrays with stable row identity
description: Add, reorder and remove rows of a flat string array while keeping native, JavaScript-free submission working.
---

<script>
	import { Callout } from "$lib/markdown";
</script>

Primitive arrays submit as repeated flat input names, without JSON encoding. Stable row IDs keep DOM nodes with their values; after validation, the application must also move index-based errors and taint with those rows.

## Schema

```ts title="src/routes/urls/schema.ts"
import { z } from "zod/v3";

export const urlsSchema = z.object({
	urls: z.array(z.string().url("Enter a valid URL.")).min(1, "Add at least one URL."),
});

export type UrlsData = z.infer<typeof urlsSchema>;
```

## Server

`ElementField` uses `urls[N]` to select a row, but renders the repeated parent name `urls` for native submission. Superforms parses those repeated values into the array.

```ts title="src/routes/urls/+page.server.ts"
import { fail } from "@sveltejs/kit";
import { message, superValidate } from "sveltekit-superforms";
import { zod } from "sveltekit-superforms/adapters";
import { urlsSchema } from "./schema.js";

export const load = async () => ({
	form: await superValidate(
		{ urls: ["https://a.example", "https://b.example"] },
		zod(urlsSchema)
	),
});

export const actions = {
	default: async ({ request }) => {
		const form = await superValidate(request, zod(urlsSchema));
		return form.valid ? message(form, "URLs saved.") : fail(400, { form });
	},
};
```

## Form

The complete [array recipe](https://github.com/emmorts/formsnap/blob/main/packages/formsnap/src/routes/arrays/+page.svelte) supports native and enhanced submissions. Its row keys and explicit control IDs come from application-owned identity, not the current index or value.

```svelte title="src/routes/urls/+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { onMount, tick, untrack } from "svelte";
	import { superForm, type SuperValidated } from "sveltekit-superforms";
	import { Control, ElementField, Fieldset, Label, Legend } from "@emmorts/formsnap";
	import type { UrlsData } from "./schema.js";

	let {
		data,
		form: action,
	}: {
		data: { form: SuperValidated<UrlsData> };
		form?: { form: SuperValidated<UrlsData> } | null;
	} = $props();
	const validated = untrack(() => action?.form ?? data.form);
	const form = superForm(
		untrack(() => data.form),
		{
			resetForm: false,
			invalidateAll: false,
			validationMethod: "submit-only",
		}
	);
	const { form: formData, errors, tainted, enhance, message, submitting } = form;
	let rowIds = $state(validated.data.urls.map((_, index) => index));
	let nextRowId = validated.data.urls.length;
	let hydrated = $state(false);
	let addButton = $state<HTMLButtonElement>();
	let mutationMessage = $state("");
	let mutationCount = 0;
	onMount(() => {
		hydrated = true;
	});

	function replaceRows(nextIds: number[]) {
		const previousIndexes: Partial<Record<number, number>> = {};
		rowIds.forEach((id, index) => {
			previousIndexes[id] = index;
		});
		const nextUrls = nextIds.map((id) => {
			const index = previousIndexes[id];
			return index === undefined ? "" : $formData.urls[index]!;
		});
		const nextErrors: NonNullable<typeof $errors.urls> = {};
		const nextTaint: NonNullable<typeof $tainted> = { urls: {} };
		nextIds.forEach((id, index) => {
			const previousIndex = previousIndexes[id];
			if (previousIndex !== undefined && $errors.urls?.[previousIndex]) {
				nextErrors[index] = $errors.urls[previousIndex];
			}
			const rowTaint = previousIndex === undefined ? true : $tainted?.urls?.[previousIndex];
			if (rowTaint !== undefined) nextTaint.urls![index] = rowTaint;
		});
		rowIds = nextIds;
		formData.update((data) => ({ ...data, urls: nextUrls }), { taint: false });
		tainted.set(nextTaint);
		errors.set({ ...$errors, urls: nextErrors }, { force: true });
	}

	function announce(change: string) {
		mutationMessage = `Update ${++mutationCount}: ${change} ${rowIds.length} ${rowIds.length === 1 ? "row" : "rows"} remaining.`;
	}

	async function focusRow(id: number | undefined) {
		await tick();
		if (id === undefined) addButton?.focus();
		else document.getElementById(`array-url-${id}`)?.focus();
	}

	async function addRow() {
		const id = nextRowId++;
		replaceRows([...rowIds, id]);
		announce(`Added URL ${rowIds.length}.`);
		await focusRow(id);
	}

	async function reorderRows() {
		if (rowIds.length < 2) return;
		const active = document.activeElement;
		replaceRows([...rowIds].reverse());
		announce("Reversed the row order.");
		await tick();
		if (active instanceof HTMLElement && active.isConnected) active.focus();
	}

	async function removeRow(id = rowIds[rowIds.length - 1]) {
		if (id === undefined) return;
		const index = rowIds.indexOf(id);
		if (index < 0) return;
		const recoverFocus = document
			.getElementById(`array-row-${id}`)
			?.contains(document.activeElement);
		replaceRows(rowIds.filter((rowId) => rowId !== id));
		announce(`Removed URL ${index + 1}.`);
		if (recoverFocus) await focusRow(rowIds[index] ?? rowIds[index - 1]);
	}
</script>

<form method="POST" use:enhance novalidate>
	<Fieldset {form} name="urls" fieldErrors>
		<Legend>Website URLs</Legend>
		{#snippet description()}Enter one URL per row.{/snippet}
		{#each $formData.urls as _, index (rowIds[index])}
			<div id={`array-row-${rowIds[index]}`}>
				<ElementField {form} name={`urls[${index}]` as `urls[${number}]`} fieldErrors>
					<Control id={`array-url-${rowIds[index]}`}>
						{#snippet children({ props })}
							<Label>URL {index + 1}</Label>
							<input {...props} bind:value={$formData.urls[index]} />
						{/snippet}
					</Control>
				</ElementField>
				<button
					type="button"
					aria-label={`Remove URL ${index + 1}`}
					disabled={!hydrated || $submitting}
					onclick={() => removeRow(rowIds[index])}>Remove row</button
				>
			</div>
		{/each}
	</Fieldset>
	<button type="button" bind:this={addButton} disabled={!hydrated || $submitting} onclick={addRow}
		>Add row</button
	>
	<button
		type="button"
		disabled={!hydrated || $submitting || rowIds.length < 2}
		onclick={reorderRows}>Reorder rows</button
	>
	<button
		type="button"
		disabled={!hydrated || $submitting || rowIds.length === 0}
		onclick={() => removeRow()}>Remove row</button
	>
	<div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">{mutationMessage}</div>
	<button type="submit">Save URLs</button>
</form>

{#if $message}<p role="status">{$message}</p>{/if}
```

## How it works

- Native submission still works without JavaScript. Enhancement preserves the current document and row identities; row-management buttons are disabled until hydration and while submitting.
- `replaceRows` moves submitted row errors and current row taint alongside values. Forced error-store replacement removes deleted numeric slots. This example has only the `urls` field; preserve other fields' taint when adapting it to a larger schema.
- Row errors remain until the next save, even if the user edits the value. Structural mutations clear collection-level errors because membership or order has changed; only the next server validation establishes which errors still apply.
- Added rows receive focus. Deleting the active row focuses the next row, otherwise the previous row, otherwise Add row. Deleting an unfocused row does not steal focus.
- One persistent polite region reports mutations. A sequence distinguishes repeated operations; automated checks verify the DOM updates, not screen-reader speech.
- `resetForm: false` and `invalidateAll: false` keep successful enhanced submissions from replacing the edited list. `novalidate` demonstrates server errors rather than blocking invalid URLs in the browser.

<Callout type="warning">

Do not key rows by their value or by the row object. Duplicate values collide as keys, and Superforms swaps row objects during taint updates — both make Svelte reuse the wrong DOM node, scrambling input bindings and focus.

</Callout>

<Callout type="note">

This recipe is the JavaScript-free alternative to [nested data](/docs/recipes/nested-data). Object rows need JSON enhancement. If several array forms share a page, give each form its own row/control ID prefix.

</Callout>
